(* README *)

1 - Overview
    --------

    This directory contains the formal theory packages of Proofcase Export.

    A##  Algorithmic contributions: algorithms and effective methods.

    L##  Lemmatic contributions: lemmas, theorems, reductions, metatheorems, 
         separations, and reusable formal gadgets.

    M##  Model contributions: full formal models, logics, proof theories,
         metatheories, and self-contained formal systems.

    P##  Problem-solving contributions: achieved proofs of named open problems,
         conjectures, challenges, or externally specified mathematical targets.

    S##  Semantic support packages: semantics, interpretations, realizability
         translations, models of problem meaning, and interfaces explaining how
         an external statement is represented inside a formal development.

2 - Canonicals
    ----------

    Each theory package is presented as a sequential formal development. The
    early files introduce premises, definitions, and implementation lemmas; the
    later files expose theorem interfaces, examples, and generated artifacts.

    The following file roles are reserved for package-level boundaries:

      00_Premises       Shared imports, vocabulary, and neutral definitions.
      91_Multiplexing/  Obligations and exports controlled by a switch.
      92_Constructor    Construction of payloads from theorem surface.
      93_Construct/     Concrete export-facing payload.
      94_IO             Effective Input/Output.
      95_API            Stable import surface for other packages.
      96_QED            Final theorem closure for the package and reports.
      97_Artifacts      Ocaml artifact extraction commands.
      98_Sanity         Local consistency and smoke checks.
      98_Sanity/        Local consistency and smoke checks for a payload.
      99_Exposition     Examples and demonstrations.

    Note that not every package contains every boundary file.

    File order follows proof dependency and computational cost. Expensive
    artifact generation is isolated near the end of a package, after the
    mathematical theorem surface it reports on.


3 - Index
    -----

    A001

      CARRYLESS PAIRING

      Certified pairing and unpairing of natural numbers using the Fibonacci
      base.

    M001

      REGULATOR THEORY

      A constructive framework for finite, syntactic, Boolean-checkable
      derivability between objects.

    S001

      ROCQ TUTORIAL

      First-contact tutorial examples for terms, computation, tiny data types,
      proof scripts, proof terms, and Curry-Howard implication.

    S002

      GENERAL LOGIC FORMULARY

      A compact reference formulary of reusable logical proof patterns,
      starting with elementary propositional reasoning and quantifiers.

    S003

      PIGEONHOLE DIVISIBILITY ERDŐS-PÓLYA ANECDOTE

      A formal proof of the Erdős-Pólya anecdote that among any `n + 1`
      distinct positive integers chosen from `1` through `2n`, two are related
      by divisibility.

    S004

      RULE 30 CENTER-COLUMN REDUCTION CONTRACT

      A self-contained Rule 30 base semantics and a closed proof of the
      center-column periodicity reduction contract. The package does not prove
      the unconditional center-column nonperiodicity claim; it exposes the
      center-tail-to-window lift obligation as the remaining dependency.
